# Backend wiring for the Angel mint. Copy to .env and fill in.
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored - real endpoints/creds never go in the repo.
#
# From inside the container, host.docker.internal reaches services running on
# your host (the compose sets this up). If BTC/Counterparty run as other
# containers, use their service names on a shared docker network instead.

# ── Network ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mainnet | testnet4 | signet. Drives wallet provider, explorer links, and
# which <NETWORK>_* overrides below take effect.
BTC_NETWORK=mainnet

# ── Bitcoin Core (BTC) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Needs txindex=1. Auth: set USER+PASSWORD (recommended in Docker), OR point
# BTC_COOKIE_FILE at a bind-mounted .cookie. User/password wins if both set.
BTC_RPC_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8332
BTC_RPC_USER=rpc_user
BTC_RPC_PASSWORD=rpc_password
# BTC_COOKIE_FILE=/root/.bitcoin/.cookie   # only if you bind-mount the cookie

# ── Counterparty (XCP) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Counterparty Core v2 API.
CP_API_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4000

# ── Wiring both chains at once (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# <NETWORK>_<NAME> overrides the plain var for that network, so you can keep
# mainnet + testnet4 configured side by side and switch with BTC_NETWORK alone.
# TESTNET4_BTC_RPC_URL=http://host.docker.internal:48332
# TESTNET4_BTC_RPC_USER=rpc_user
# TESTNET4_BTC_RPC_PASSWORD=rpc_password
# TESTNET4_CP_API_URL=http://host.docker.internal:44000

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
COUNTER_DATA_DIR=/data

# Optional: AI assist routes (/ai/*). Not needed to mint.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: only if you switch the tunnel to a named/account Cloudflare tunnel.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=
